# Response headers for the Cloudflare asset layer.
#
# Like .assetsignore, this must land inside the assets directory, so it lives in
# public/ and next build copies it into out/. Wrangler does not upload it as an
# asset; it is read as configuration.
#
# Rules are additive: a file under _next/static matches both blocks below and
# is served the headers from each.

# Reach this origin over HTTPS only, for a year, and refuse to fall back to
# http:// even if a link or a typed address asks for it.
#
# This is the durable half of HTTPS enforcement — it moves the upgrade into the
# browser, so a repeat visit never puts a plaintext request on the wire to be
# intercepted. The other half is the zone's "Always Use HTTPS" redirect, which
# is what covers a visitor's *first* request, before any HSTS policy is cached.
# Neither replaces the other; see "HTTPS" in README.md.
#
# includeSubDomains is safe here: the zone serves web content on the apex only
# (www has no record), and Email Routing's MX/SPF records are untouched — HSTS
# governs HTTP, not mail.
#
# Deliberately not `preload`. That hardcodes the domain into browser binaries
# and takes months to unwind; a max-age expires on its own.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Everything under _next/static is content-hashed by the build — a change to the
# file changes its name — so it can be cached permanently. Without this, the
# Workers default (max-age=0, must-revalidate) forces a conditional request per
# chunk on every repeat visit.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Deliberately not listed: HTML, the CV PDF, and the icons/og image in public/.
# None are content-hashed, so they keep the revalidate-always default and a
# replaced file goes live immediately.
